message.content:
Here’s how you’d query VirusTotal for the sub‑domain relationships of **example.org** using your API key (`my_api`), limiting the results to 10 items and starting at the cursor `abc`:

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects?relationship_type=subdomains&limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc
Authorization: Bearer my_api
Accept: application/json
```

If the request succeeds, the API will return a JSON payload similar to the following (the actual IDs and context attributes will depend on the current data in VirusTotal):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": {
          "harmless": 12,
          "malicious": 0,
          "suspicious": 0,
          "undetected": 5,
          "timeout": 0
        },
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000000,
        "last_analysis_results": { /* detailed engine results */ }
      },
      "relationships": { /* relationships to other objects */ }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": {
          "harmless": 8,
          "malicious": 1,
          "suspicious": 0,
          "undetected": 7,
          "timeout": 0
        },
        "last_analysis_date": 1699999000,
        "last_analysis_results": { /* detailed engine results */ }
      },
      "relationships": { /* relationships to other objects */ }
    }
    /* up to 10 items total */
  ],
  "meta": {
    "continuation_token": "defghijklmnop"
  }
}
```

From this response you would extract only the `id` and any `context_attributes` you’re interested in. For example, if you only care about the IDs and the last‑analysis stats, you could transform the data into a concise list like:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "sub1.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "last_analysis_stats": {
        "harmless": 12,
        "malicious": 0,
        "suspicious": 0,
        "undetected": 5,
        "timeout": 0
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "sub2.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "last_analysis_stats": {
        "harmless": 8,
        "malicious": 1,
        "suspicious": 0,
        "undetected": 7,
        "timeout": 0
      }
    }
  }
]
```

(Replace the placeholder values with the actual data returned by the API.)
